.TH XDCP 1 "October 2026" "xcat-ports 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xdcp \- concurrently copy files to or from multiple cluster nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xdcp
\fInoderange\fR
[\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-ignore\-host\-key\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-separator\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIfanout\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fItimeout\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR]
[\fB\-P\fR]
[\fB\-R\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIcommand\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
[\fB\-\-sudo\fR]
[\fB\-\-nodestatus\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR]
[\fB\-Q\fR]
[\fB\-B\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR]
\fIsourcefile...\fR \fItargetpath\fR
.PP
.B xdcp
\fInoderange\fR
[\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-ignore\-host\-key\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-separator\fR]
[\fB\-l\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIfanout\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fItimeout\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIcommand\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
[\fB\-\-sudo\fR]
[\fB\-\-nodestatus\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR]
[\fB\-Q\fR]
\fB\-F\fR \fIsynclist_file\fR
.PP
.B xdcp
[\fB\-i\fR \fIinstall_image\fR]
\fB\-F\fR \fIsynclist_file\fR
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
[\fB\-T\fR]
.PP
.B xdcp
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-q\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xdcp
is a standalone port of xCAT's \fBxdcp\fR utility running in bypass mode
(without requiring the \fBxcatd\fR daemon or an xCAT database). It resolves
the target \fInoderange\fR locally and copies files in parallel across all
matching nodes using \fBrsync\fR(1) or OpenSSH \fBscp\fR(1).
.PP
.B xdcp
supports four primary operating modes:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPush Mode\fR (default): Copies one or more local files or directories to each target node.
If multiple source files are specified, \fItargetpath\fR is treated as a remote directory.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPull Mode\fR (\fB\-P\fR): Pulls a file or directory from each remote node into a local directory \fItargetpath\fR.
To distinguish files from different nodes, the remote node's name is appended to the filename as
\fB\fIfilename\fR._\fItarget\fR\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSynclist Mode\fR (\fB\-F\fR): Distributes files according to mappings specified in a synclist file.
Supports optional per-line node filter ranges.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBImage Mode\fR (\fB\-i\fR): Synchronizes files directly into a local operating system installation root directory.
.PP
Output from each node is buffered and prefixed with \fB\fInode\fR: \fR.
When copying across multiple nodes, outputs from different hosts are separated by an empty line
for readability (can be suppressed with \fB\-\-no\-separator\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-host\-key\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-hostkey\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR, \fB\-\-no\-host\-key\-check\fR
Disable SSH host key verification for underlying \fBssh\fR, \fBscp\fR, and \fBrsync\fR commands.
Configures:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o StrictHostKeyChecking=no\fR (accept unknown host keys automatically)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\fR (ignore user known_hosts file)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o GlobalKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\fR (ignore system known_hosts file)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-o LogLevel=ERROR\fR (suppress host key warnings on stderr)
.RE
.IP
Can also be enabled globally via the \fBXDCP_IGNORE_HOST_KEY\fR, \fBXDSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY\fR, or \fBDSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY\fR environment variables.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-separator\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sep\fR, \fB\-\-noseparator\fR
Do not print an empty line separator between outputs from different hosts.
Can also be set via the \fBXDCP_NO_SEPARATOR\fR, \fBXDSH_NO_SEPARATOR\fR, or \fBDSH_NO_SEPARATOR\fR environment variables.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-pull\fR
Pulls files from the remote targets and places them into the local directory \fItargetpath\fR.
The target path must be an existing directory on the local host.
Only a single source file or directory (with \fB\-R\fR) can be specified.
The copied file or directory is saved as \fB\fItargetpath\fR/\fIbasename\fR._\fItarget\fR\fR.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-File\fR \fIsynclist_file\fR
Specifies the path to an xCAT synclist file defining file synchronization mappings.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-rootimg\fR \fIinstall_image\fR
Specifies the path to a local Linux root image directory. When used with \fB\-F\fR,
files are synchronized locally into \fIinstall_image\fR without executing remote commands.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
Recursively copy directories to the remote targets, or recursively pull directories with \fB\-P\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-preserve\fR
Preserve source file characteristics (permissions and modification timestamps).
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-node\-rcp\fR \fIcommand\fR
Path to the remote copy command (\fBrsync\fR or \fBscp\fR).
If not specified, \fBrsync\fR is used by default if available in \fBPATH\fR; otherwise \fBscp\fR is used.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fanout\fR \fIfanout\fR
Maximum number of concurrent remote copy processes to run in parallel. Default is \fB64\fR (configurable via \fBDSH_FANOUT\fR).
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIuser\fR
Remote login user ID. Defaults to current user (or \fBDSH_TO_USERID\fR).
A \fIuser\fR@\fInoderange\fR prefix on the noderange argument is also supported.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-node\-options\fR \fIoptions\fR
Additional options passed directly to the remote copy command.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR
Inactivity timeout in seconds (default \fB5\fR, \fB0\fR = unlimited).
.TP
\fB\-\-sudo\fR
Executes remote copy commands with \fBsudo\fR privileges (using \fB\-\-rsync\-path='sudo rsync'\fR for rsync).
.TP
\fB\-\-nodestatus\fR
Output a status line for each node: \fB\fInode\fR: Remote_copy_successful\fR or \fB\fInode\fR: Remote_copy_failed, error_code=\fIN\fR.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-monitor\fR
Display progress messages as copy commands start and finish on each node.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-trace\fR
Print diagnostic command invocations during execution.
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-exit\-status\fR
Print exit code summary for each node (\fB\fInode\fR: Remote_copy_rc = \fIN\fR).
.TP
\fB\-Q\fR, \fB\-\-silent\fR
Silent mode. Suppress standard output and standard error from remote commands.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR, \fB\-\-bypass\fR
Bypass mode (accepted for compatibility; this standalone port always runs in bypass mode).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR
Sync service nodes flag (accepted for compatibility).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display command usage and exit.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-show\-config\fR
Display configuration parameters and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.SH SYNCLIST FILE FORMAT
A synclist file specifies source files on the local host and destination paths on target nodes:
.IP
.nf
\fI/path/src_file1\fR \fB->\fR \fI/path/dst_file\fR
\fI/path/src_file1\fR \fI/path/src_file2\fR \fB->\fR \fI/path/dst_dir/\fR
\fI/path/src_dir/*\fR \fB->\fR \fI/path/dst_dir/\fR
\fI/path/src_file\fR \fB->\fR (\fInoderange\fR) \fI/path/dst_file\fR
.fi
.PP
Lines starting with \fB#\fR and blank lines are ignored.
Wildcard patterns (\fB*\fR, \fB?\fR) in source paths are expanded on the local host.
An optional target node filter \fB(\fInoderange\fB)\fR can restrict synchronization of specific lines to matching nodes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDCP_IGNORE_HOST_KEY, XDSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY, DSH_IGNORE_HOST_KEY
When set to \fB1\fR, \fBtrue\fR, \fByes\fR, or \fBon\fR, enables \fB\-k\fR host key ignoring by default.
.TP
.B XDCP_NO_SEPARATOR, XDSH_NO_SEPARATOR, DSH_NO_SEPARATOR
When set to \fB1\fR, \fBtrue\fR, \fByes\fR, or \fBon\fR, disables the blank line separator between outputs of different hosts.
.TP
.B DSH_FANOUT
Default fanout value (concurrency level). Defaults to \fB64\fR.
.TP
.B DSH_TIMEOUT
Default command inactivity timeout in seconds (defaults to \fB5\fR; \fB0\fR disables timeout).
.TP
.B DSH_TO_USERID
Default remote user ID if not specified via \fB\-l\fR.
.TP
.B DSH_NODE_RCP
Default remote copy executable.
.TP
.B DSH_NODE_OPTS, DSH_REMOTE_OPTS
Default options to pass to the remote copy command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is equal to the number of failed target nodes (0 if all targets succeeded).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
1. Copy \fB/etc/hosts\fR to all nodes in \fBnode[1-10]\fR:
.B xdcp node[1-10] /etc/hosts /etc/hosts
.TP
2. Pull \fB/etc/hosts\fR from all nodes into local directory \fB/tmp/hosts.dir\fR:
.B xdcp node[1-10] -P /etc/hosts /tmp/hosts.dir
Each file is saved as \fB/tmp/hosts.dir/hosts._node1\fR, \fB/tmp/hosts.dir/hosts._node2\fR, etc.
.TP
3. Recursively pull directory \fB/var/log/app\fR from nodes into \fB/tmp/logs\fR:
.B xdcp node[1-4] -RP /var/log/app /tmp/logs
Saved as \fB/tmp/logs/app._node1\fR, \fB/tmp/logs/app._node2\fR, etc.
.TP
4. Sync files to compute nodes using a synclist file:
.B xdcp compute -F /tmp/myrsync
.TP
5. Sync files directly into an OS installation root image:
.B xdcp -i /install/netboot/fedora/rootimg -F /tmp/myrsync
.TP
6. Copy files with ignored host keys and custom rsync options:
.B xdcp -k node[1-8] -o "-v --progress" /local/file /remote/file
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdsh (1),
.BR pping (1),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR scp (1)
